{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471779-scp-items-in-vtm-duped-by-thaumaturgy","id":1471779,"title":"SCP items in VTM duped by Thaumaturgy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-04T08:39:38-08:00","id":1471779,"title":"SCP items in VTM duped by Thaumaturgy?","content":"My character is a Malkavian who knows a fair bit about Thaumaturgy and I got to thinking. The SCP as seen here: <a href=\"https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-604\" target=\"_blank\">https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-604</a> the glasses of which turn red wine or other fluids into human blood. Would Tremere Thaumaturgy be able to dupe this object for that use? Or do they have another technique that does that same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18963-chris313allnight","name":"Chris313AllNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T17:25:47-08:00","id":1471884,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you mean by &quot;that use&quot;.<br /> <br /> Blood artificially created does not nourish a vampire. It doesn't matter if it is created with science or magic, unless it is imbued with extra magical energy, which in Vampire terms would mean Vitae anyway, on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <br /> Yet, AFAIK such artificial blood can be consumed without deleterious effects, so if its purpose lies beyond vampiric nourishment, sure, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T15:41:38-08:00","id":1471955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471779-scp-items-in-vtm-duped-by-thaumaturgy?p=1471884#post1471884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what you mean by &quot;that use&quot;.<br /> <br /> Blood artificially created does not nourish a vampire. It doesn't matter if it is created with science or magic, unless it is imbued with extra magical energy, which in Vampire terms would mean Vitae anyway, on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <br /> Yet, AFAIK such artificial blood can be consumed without deleterious effects, so if its purpose lies beyond vampiric nourishment, sure, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pardon me for not being clearer. I wanted to know if Thaumaturgy could be used to recreate the glassware of this object for use in feeding a vamp, since you can pour things like red wine or even juices into the glasses and it becomes human blood. Would that feed a vamp? Or be usable in rituals? Hell, one thought I had was that could something like this be used for blood transfusions to take care of one's Ghouls when they've been drained of blood like 2BP in or more and need blood to recover?<br /> <br /> Hope that is clearer. Thank you for your answers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18963-chris313allnight","name":"Chris313AllNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T00:27:35-08:00","id":1471985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris313AllNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471779-scp-items-in-vtm-duped-by-thaumaturgy?p=1471955#post1471955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon me for not being clearer. I wanted to know if Thaumaturgy could be used to recreate the glassware of this object for use in feeding a vamp, since you can pour things like red wine or even juices into the glasses and it becomes human blood. Would that feed a vamp? Or be usable in rituals? Hell, one thought I had was that could something like this be used for blood transfusions to take care of one's Ghouls when they've been drained of blood like 2BP in or more and need blood to recover?<br /> <br /> Hope that is clearer. Thank you for your answers</div> </div> </div> </div>That's clearer, yet I already answered, but I'll also try to be clearer:<br /> <br /> 1 - <b>To feed a Vampire</b>: it wouldn't do. A vampire can drink this blood, but won't gain any Blood Point in the process;<br /> <br /> 2 - <b>Be usable in rituals</b>: wouldn't do. Magic rituals by default discard magically created fuel as suitable replacement;<br /> <br /> 3 - <b>For blood transfusion</b>: it would do, as completely normal human blood. You would still need the medical equipment and skill to do the transfusion, and the receiver would still need time to recover, but it would work.<br /> <br /> <b>Caveat</b>: a blood transfusion replenishes the blood itself quickly, but the weakness of the body does not goes away as fast. In game terms it counts just as proper medical treatment, but won't heal the damage suffered in the process that caused blood loss any faster than that. It is a very good medical treatment and may even make a Blood Doll able to be fed on more frequently in a month, but won't make for a fast replenishment of blood reserves in a short time frame.<br /> <br /> If you try to give this blood to the Ghoul/Blood Doll just to suck them again, they'll die from the damage all the same.<br /> <br /> <b>My suggestion</b>: even if this blood does not confers Blood Points, you can make it still viable as delivery for drugs and whatnot, or just with curious taste. You can try to make something out of the <i>experience</i> it offers, which would be pretty cool by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T10:05:30-08:00","id":1472006,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was using this primary for feeding, so that's a bust. Slept on it and didn't think the rituals thing would work either. As you say, I'm thinking of using this for blood transfusion since our coterie has the knowledge. The blood for experience thing is interesting. Reminds me of the bit in the book that says vamps can get drunk or high if they take blood that has their drug of choice in it. Thanks for the suggestion. I'm gonna talk it over with my group and see what they thing of these possibilities.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your time and help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18963-chris313allnight","name":"Chris313AllNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T11:24:05-08:00","id":1472011,"title":"","content":"[well i dont know... i just delete this because discussion is dead]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 04-17-2022, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}